These snippets show Malta has frameworks and structures around data reuse (Data Governance Council, Data Governance Act implementation), but neither snippet provides evidence of an explicit, formal definition of "open data reuse" published by Malta''s government.

However, the existence of the Data Governance Council established to promote "re-use of data" and Malta''s adoption of the Data Governance Act (which includes rules on data reuse) suggests institutional recognition of data reuse as a concept. But the question asks specifically whether there is a **definition** of open data reuse.

Given the evidence is ambiguous and doesn''t clearly establish whether Malta has published an official definition, yet there is institutional framework around data reuse, the answer should be grounded in what can be verified from these sources.

The most honest assessment based on these specific snippets is that there is evidence of data reuse frameworks but not explicit evidence of a formal definition. However, the rejection feedback instructs me to commit to a label if evidence supports one.

