ed from this survey relate to the purpose of using NSO data, quality of NSO data in comparison with statistics produced by other organisations, trust of users in NSO st", "title": "User Satisfaction Survey - NSO Malta", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://msdi.data.gov.mt/", "snippet": "The Malta Spatial Data Infrastructure (MSDI) is a portal that offers web services to the general public, public service and public sector organisations. MSDI is aimed at sharing environmental related geospatial datasets. This service facilitates public service organisations that do not have the necessary infrastructure to host spatial datasets files on the web server and make them available to the general public. ... On the receiving end the general public may: view the spatial datasets using online displaying tools, use the Discovery Service to perform online search for datasets based on metadata, and request download of datasets that are available on the website through the Download Service.", "title": "Malta Spatial Data Infrastructure", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://nso.gov.mt/statistics-portals/", "snippet": "These statistics portals represent a significant shift from traditional publications to dynamic, continuously updated online platforms. This change is part of a broader strategy to improve the timeliness and accessibility of statistical information. ... Data tables are provided in Excel format, making them easier to download and analyse. The portals also feature interactive charts, which can be downloaded along with the underlying data for use in media or other publications.", "title": "Statistics Portals - NSO Malta", "provider": "diy"}]');
