o", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://intarch.ac.uk/journal/issue59/2/full-text.html", "snippet": "A survey by the European Archaeological Council (EAC) in 2017 addressed practices of decision-making in archaeological heritage management, including how fieldwork documentation is being archived and published. Based on the responses of 22 representatives of EAC member states and regions the survey report concluded that \"Lack of policies on digital archives is common\". The survey found that storage of physical objects is quite well established as over 75% of respondents said that objects are pla ... The COST Action SEADDA involves ARIADNEplus partners and institutions from several additional countries, with representation from nearly all European nations as well as wider international participation (Argentina, Canada, Israel, Japan, Turkey, Pakistan and the United States). The SEADDA network supports institutions seeking to develop archaeological data repositories that take account of heritage regulations, and which are able to curate and make accessible varied and complex data. ... In 2019, the 2013 Directive was replaced by the Directive (EU) 2019/1024 on Open Data and the Reuse of Public Sector Information, also called the Open Data Directive. This Directive has been in force since 16 July 2019, and was to be incorporated by Member States into national law by 16 July 2021 at the latest. For the repository survey, Article 10 of the Open Data Directive is important. This aims to make research data funded, collected or generated by public sector bodies openly accessible and", "title": "Data Management Policies and Practices of Digital ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.archives.gov/preservation/digital-preservation/linked-data", "snippet": "NARA''s Digital Preservation Unit has been collaborating closely with colleagues at other national archives and libraries as well as with the WikiData for Digital Preservation initiative to make our Digital Preservation Framework available as a Linked Open Data Resource to complement the preservation plans made available on GitHub. The Framework provides Preservation Plans for several hundred formats, including links to specifications and standards, links to community documentation about the form", "title": "Digital Preservation Framework Linked Open Data", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://dag.cessda.eu/Chapter-2/2-Preservation-Policies", "snippet": "A digital preservation policy is a part of the preservation environment of the data archive. Its content includes the information about (i) an organizational framework in terms of the mission, selection and acquisition, access and use of data; (ii) potential challenges such as legal issues or the role of technological progress; (iii) principles for the guidelines of the data preservation like the main strategy, principles in terms of standards and co\u2010operation, well\u2010documented and traceable proc", "title": "2.2 Preservation Policies - DAG", "provider": "diy"}]');
