 "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/nieuws-internationaal", "snippet": "Economische impact: alhoewel het EU gemiddelde marginaal omhoog is gegaan van 61% in 2016 naar 65% in 2017, is Nederland van 75% naar 100% gegaan doordat verschillende studies zijn gepubliceerd in de afgelopen 2 jaar die de economische impact van Open Data op de maatschappij hebben onderzocht.", "title": "Nieuws internationaal | Data overheid - Overheid.nl", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/ondersteuning/open-data/beleid", "snippet": "Een open overheid kan bijdragen aan oplossingen voor maatschappelijke vraagstukken, is een kernwaarde van de democratische rechtstaat, komt tegemoet aan de veranderende samenleving en heeft economische waarde.", "title": "Open data beleid | Data overheid - Overheid.nl", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/assessment-impact-data-2021", "snippet": "This page provides an assessment on the impact of the data that is available on data.overheid.nl. The assessment follows the structure of the EU maturity report 2021 for measuring the impact of data.", "title": "Assessment of the Impact of data 2021 - Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/impact-en", "snippet": "Impact is the effect that opening open data for reuse has to solve economic and social problems. Data.overheid.nl has several instruments to give insight in the impact of data: the applications that are developed using data; the high value datasets and statistics.", "title": "Impact of data | Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/ondersteuning/open-data/beleid", "snippet": "An open government can contribute to solutions for social issues, is a core value of the democratic constitutional state, responds to a changing society and has economic value.", "title": "Open data policy | Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/dataset/52684-production-process--economic-activity--region--national-accounts", "snippet": "This table contains figures of the Regional accounts. Regional accounts are consistent with National accounts, except for differences due to rounding, and also with Eurostat''s European System of National and Regional Accounts 2010 (ESA 2010). The new Standard Industrial Classification 2008 (SIC 2008) is used in the National and Regional Accounts of the Netherlands. ... Data available from: 1995 Status of the figures: The figures of the year 1995 to 2022 are final. Data of the year 2023 are also final, but the figures on Labour input of employed persons and Labour input of employees are an exception, due to the late availability of annual data on self-employed persons.", "title": "Production process; economic activity, region, National Accounts", "provider": "diy"}]');
