ector Information. PSI wordt tegenwoordig ook wel ''open data'' genoemd. De Europese PSI- of Open Data richtlijn roept overheden op om zoveel mogelijk data herbruikbaar aan te bieden.", "title": "PSI richtlijnen | Data overheid - Overheid.nl", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/ondersteuning/open-data/dcat", "snippet": "Data.overheid.nl then delivers to the European data portal in DCAT format.", "title": "DCAT-AP-DONL - Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/assessment-impact-data-2021", "snippet": "This page provides an assessment on the impact of the data that is available on data.overheid.nl. The assessment follows the structure of the EU maturity report 2021 for measuring the impact of data.", "title": "Assessment of the Impact of data 2021 - Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "http://data.overheid.nl/en/ondersteuning/open-data/begrippenkader", "snippet": "High value datasets are datasets that hold significant value for society. These are made available with priority by government organisations and are also published on data.overheid.nl. A distinction is made between two types of high value datasets:\nHoogwaardige dataset | EU: datasets that belong to one of the categories established by the European Union as important datasets. More information can be found at http://data.overheid.nl/hoogwaardige-dataset.", "title": "Relevant concepts - Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/dataset/4244-government-revenue--transactions--sectors", "snippet": "This table contains information on the revenue of the general government sector. The terms and definitions used are in accordance with the framework of National Accounts. National Accounts are based on the international definitions of the European System of Accounts (ESA 2010).", "title": "Government revenue; transactions, sectors - Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/dataset/4269-trust-in-others--legal-system-and-politics--european-comparison", "snippet": "This table provides information on how much inhabitants of various European countries aged 15 years or older trust other people, the legal system and politics. Figures are from 2002 onwards. The question concerning trust in other people is: Overall, do you think most people can be trusted, or that you can''t be too careful?. Trust in the legal system and politics is determined by asking people how much they trust a number of political and organisational institutions, viz. national parliament, the", "title": "Trust in others, legal system and politics; European comparison", "provider": "diy"}]');
