Snippet [1] mentions "strategies to improve citizens understanding of the use and application of the Open Data Portal and increase accessibility to citizens" – this is about access to existing government data, not incentivizing citizen data generation.

Snippets [2], [3], and [4] discuss general open data governance, chatbot services, and e-government initiatives, but none address incentives for citizens to publish their own data.

The previous rejection correctly identified that the earlier citation was about citizen access/participation in government data, not citizen-generated data publication. The current search results similarly lack evidence of measures to incentivize citizen-generated data.

