hip.org/stories/lessons-from-reformers-albania-publishes-local-government-legislation-online/", "snippet": "A civil-society driven reform has led to all 61 of Albania''s municipalities publishing municipal council decisions online on a central platform.", "title": "Lessons from Reformers: Albania Publishes Local ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://decentralization.net/2024/06/local-government-in-albania-a-status-report-for-2023/", "snippet": "A recently published report on Local Government in Albania prepared by the Institute for Municipalities for Albania emphasized the vital role of local developments in the growth of local communities and history. The annual status report serves as a model of transparency, encouraging accountability and integrity among municipal employees. It evaluates national-scale results, compares municipalities, and promotes local leadership in areas such as service quality, budget expenditures, tax collectio", "title": "Local Government in Albania: A Status Report for 2023", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-95674-4_2", "snippet": "Decentralisation in Albania aims to strengthen local government by transferring authority and resources from the central to local government to improve governance and service delivery. Local governments partly manage essential services such as education, health, infrastructure, and economic development, directly addressing local needs. This change increases accountability, promotes community engagement, and ensures efficient use of resources, fostering a more inclusive approach to governance.", "title": "Albania | Springer Nature Link", "provider": "diy"}]');
