I understand the Verifier wants a committed label, but the hard rules require a verbatim quote from an admissible source that grounds the specific claim about **data.gov.mt**. The provided snippets contain no such evidence—one is a forbidden source (EDP) and the other is about the US data.gov. Fabricating a "yes" or "no" without grounding would violate rules 2, 4, and 6. `inconclusive` is the correct output given these snippets. Better search queries targeting data.gov.mt''s actual pages would be needed to reach a confident label.','2026-07-12 17:44:19','[{"provider": "diy", "ms": 875, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 1215, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 1395, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 15702, "results": 2, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 8279, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 5051, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}]','exp36_model_opus','[{"url": "https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/how-to-search/sparql/", "snippet": "SPARQL enables more advanced users to query datasets expressed in the Resource Description Framework (RDF). SPARQL can help to find specific information from a large amount of RDF dataset, even if it organized in a complex way.\nTo access the data of the European Data Portal, a machine-readable SPARQL endpoint allows querying the RDF descriptions of datasets. ... If you are not familiar with SPARQL Query Language, we invite you to read this short summary of useful SPARQL clauses which are used in the queries below. For further reading please refer to W3C recommendation. ... The following section provides a short introduction to the SPARQL language and some examples that are specific to the context of data.europa.eu.\nFor a complete documentation of the language, the specifications of SPARQL can be found on the W3C web site.", "title": "SPARQL - Documentation of the European Data Portal (EDP) - GitLab", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36812370/how-do-i-query-against-data-gov", "snippet": "SPARQL is a graph pattern language for RDF triples. A query consists of a set of \"basic graph patterns\" described by triple patterns of the form <subject>\n, <predicate>\n, <object>\n. RDF defines the subject and predicate with URI''s and the object is either a URI (object property) or literal (datatype or language-tagged property). Each triple pattern in a query must therefore have three entities. ... There is no like\nin SPARQL, but you could use a FILTER\nclause using regex\nor other string matching features of SPARQL.\nAnd please, please, please google \"SPARQL\" and \"RDF\". There is lots of information about SPARQL, and the W3C''s SPARQL 1.1 Query Language Recommendation is a comprehensive source with many good examples.", "title": "How Do I Query Against Data.gov - sparql - Stack Overflow", "provider": "diy"}]');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO phase2_researcher_runs (id,run_id,pair_run_id,question_id,country_code,retry_count,answer,answer_explanation,evidence_quote,source_url,retrieval_confidence,answer_confidence,search_queries_used,fetched_urls,domain_trust_score,language_route_used,notes,failure_mode,input_tokens,output_tokens,wall_clock_ms,estimated_cost_usd,condition_label,prompt_version_id,model_version,raw_response,created_at,search_provider_calls,experiment_id,search_snippets) VALUES (8941,'2206f8e0-e541-4243-8cd3-e3d74cb9edb3','6ee4cf5c-4376-4f9b-9563-e6b169ef6f1c','PT35','MT',3,'yes','Besides the national open data portal, Malta hosts other portals such as the NSO Regional Statistics portal offering data at the regional level for Malta, Gozo and Comino.','The Regional Statistics portal stands out as the primary source for those seeking high-quality official statistics at the regional level. It offers a structured and comprehensive overview of key socio-economic and environmental trends shaping Malta, Gozo, and Comino.','https://nso.gov.mt/regional-statistics/',0.8,0.6,'["Malta municipal open data portal Gozo", "Malta open data portal only national data.gov.mt", "Malta OGP national action plan open data portals"]','["https://nso.gov.mt/regional-statistics/", "https://portal.data.gov.mt/", "https://portal.data.gov.mt/dataset/?high_value_dataset=true", "https://msdi.data.gov.mt/", "https://opengov.gov.mt/", "https://opengov.gov.mt/maltas-national-action-plan/", "https://opengov.gov.mt/maltas-participation-in-open-government/"]',1.0,'native',NULL,NULL,4979,668,10806,0.041595,'opus_o48',22,'claude-opus-4-8','The snippets show multiple Malta portals beyond the national data.gov.mt: an NSO Regional Statistics portal and the Malta Spatial Data Infrastructure (MSDI). However, these are thematic/statistical portals, not clearly regional/local municipal open data portals. Malta is a small state with no distinct regional government layer. The MSDI is on a data.gov.mt subdomain (national). The clearest evidence is the NSO Regional Statistics portal offering data broken down by Malta, Gozo, and Comino.

