```','2026-07-12 17:44:20','[{"provider": "diy", "ms": 7999, "results": 1, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 15843, "results": 3, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 17145, "results": 3, "ok": true, "error": null}]','exp36_model_opus','[{"url": "https://nso.gov.mt/regional-statistics/", "snippet": "The Regional Statistics portal stands out as the primary source for those seeking high-quality official statistics at the regional level. It offers a structured and comprehensive overview of key socio-economic and environmental trends shaping Malta, Gozo, and Comino. Where possible, data is broken down by various socio-economic variables, enabling comparisons across different demographic groups and economic sectors. The portal encompasses eight main domains: Demography, Education, Labour Market,", "title": "Regional Statistics - NSO Malta", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://portal.data.gov.mt/", "snippet": "This version of the Malta Data Portal is designed to enable a shared platform for the management and support of metadata about Registers and Datasets emanating mainly from the laws of Malta and EU Regulations. The contents of this portal are currently works in progress and should not be considered as providing official records unless such records are confirmed through a confirmation request.", "title": "servizz pubbliku - Malta Data Portal", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://portal.data.gov.mt/dataset/?high_value_dataset=true", "snippet": "Article 17 of the Habitats Directive requires Member States to report every six years about the progress made with the implementation of the Habitats Directive, according to the biogeographical region. Malta has only one biogeographical region, this being a Mediterranean one, as represented in this dataset. ... This layer designates the Nitrate Vulnerable Zones (NVZ). At present the whole of the Maltese Islands are designated as a NVZ, as per Article 3 of Council Directive 91/676/EEC.", "title": "96 datasets found - servizz pubbliku", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://msdi.data.gov.mt/", "snippet": "The Malta Spatial Data Infrastructure (MSDI) is a portal that offers web services to the general public, public service and public sector organisations. MSDI is aimed at sharing environmental related geospatial datasets. This service facilitates public service organisations that do not have the necessary infrastructure to host spatial datasets files on the web server and make them available to the general public. ... The Planning Authority has been designated as the competent Authority in terms of the implementation of the Directive and the National Spatial Data Infrastructure in Malta.", "title": "Malta Spatial Data Infrastructure", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://opengov.gov.mt/", "snippet": "Since 2011 Malta has enhanced its contribution to open government through various initiatives, including the commitments arising from its membership in the Open Government Partnership (OGP), the introduction of e-government in order to provide better public service to the public, providing a legal framework for access of information, the launch of an open data webpage and an online public consultation platform where stakeholders and the public can participate.", "title": "Open Government Malta: Home", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://opengov.gov.mt/maltas-national-action-plan/", "snippet": "Malta launched its co-creation process to develop its 4th NAP in mid-2023 when an exercise across ministries/government entities was carried out to identify potential themes to serve as basis for discussion. Themes relating to Justice, Victims\u2019 Rights and Support and Youths were identified as possible themes. In September 2023, a call was issued inviting interested CSOs to participate in the discussions relating to the identified themes in a multi-stakeholder forum format. ... The 4th National Action Plan was submitted to the OGP on the 27th December 2023 and is now published. The reasoned response by government given in respect of the feedback received from stakeholders during the co-creation process can be found here. ... Malta has strived to implement its commitments under Malta\u2019s OGP 4th National Action Plan 2023 -2025 and will continue to ensure that these commitments are fully implemented. Furthermore, Malta is looking forward to commencing work on the development of its upcoming 5th OGP National Action Plan.", "title": "Malta''s National Action Plan - Open Government Malta", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://opengov.gov.mt/maltas-participation-in-open-government/", "snippet": "Since joining OGP, Malta submitted 3 National Action Plans (NAP) up till 2022. Due to issues in timely submission of a new action plan, in 2022, the OGP Steering Committee designated Malta as inactive in the OGP. Government has decided to reactivate its membership, by committing itself to address a number of requirements and to submit its 4th National Action Plan by December 2023. Malta submitted its 4th National Action Plan to the OGP Steering Committee on 27th December 2023 in accordance with  ... Malta joined the OGP in 2011, thereby committing to uphold the principles of open and transparent government by showing a level of citizen engagement, and enabling civil partners to have enough power to be able to deliver their message to government.", "title": "Malta''s Participation in Open Government", "provider": "diy"}]');
