- Showcasing the qualities of the data resou ... Research conducted in the Data Discoverability 2 (DD2) shows that most users of geospatial data will use search engines to find the datasets they need. This means that the metadata, which is what search engines rank, must be created in a way that is search engine optimised (SEO).", "title": "Making your data easy to find: Metadata best practice guide for data ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://msdi.data.gov.mt/", "snippet": "Organisations that have a spatial infrastructure can share spatial data through this portal using a web map services. On the receiving end the general public may: view the spatial datasets using online displaying tools, use the Discovery Service to perform online search for datasets based on metadata, and request download of datasets that are available on the website through the Download Service. ... Service metadata provides basic information about a service instance to enable the discovery of spatial data services. The description of a service includes the service type, a description of the operations and their parameters as well as information about the geographic information available from a service offering.", "title": "Malta Spatial Data Infrastructure", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://docs.open-metadata.org/v1.12.x/how-to-guides/data-discovery", "snippet": "Discovering data among thousands of datasets is hard without rich metadata and faceted search. OpenMetadata with a single catalog aggregates metadata about all data assets, and presents the right information to users depending on their needs. ... OpenMetadata provides a user-friendly interface for data discovery. OpenMetadata enables you to discover your data using a variety of strategies, including: keyword search, data associations (e.g., frequently joined tables, lineage), and complex queries.", "title": "Data Discovery | OpenMetadata How-To Guide", "provider": "diy"}]');
