```','2026-07-12 18:15:26','[{"provider": "diy", "ms": 25089, "results": 4, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 19466, "results": 1, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 17927, "results": 3, "ok": true, "error": null}]','exp36_model_opus','[{"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/ondersteuning/open-data/beleid", "snippet": "In 2019, the Ministry of the Interior and Kingdom Relations published the Government Data Agenda (''Data Agenda Overheid'') on behalf of the cabinet. This agenda follows the National Open Data Agenda. The Government Data Agenda is an intergovernmental agenda that sets out what the government will do to better deal with personal data, open data and big data. The agenda describes how data can better benefit policy-making and the solution of social issues by the government.", "title": "Open data policy | Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/assessment-impact-data-2021", "snippet": "This page provides an assessment on the impact of the data that is available on data.overheid.nl. The assessment follows the structure of the EU maturity report 2021 for measuring the impact of data.\nThe EU maturity reports, \"dimension 2\" on Open Data Impact, has the following structure:\n- Strategic awareness\n- Political Impact\n- Social Impact\n- Environmental impact\n- Economic impact", "title": "Assessment of the Impact of data 2021 - Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/ondersteuning/algemeen/over-dataoverheidnl", "snippet": "Data.overheid.nl is a register and offers help with opening and reusing government data. More information about the policy in the Netherlands regarding open data can be found here. (in Dutch) In addition descriptions of closed data can be found.\nData.overheid.nl assists government organisations in opening all available data. We also support data re-users in finding specific open data sets. Data that is not (yet) available as open data can be made available through a data request. ... The data.overheid.nl team is responsible for implementing part of the open government policy: making available data sets findable and providing support to government organisations with opening data. The Ministry of the Interior and Kingdom Relations strives to keep the quality of the data sets optimal.", "title": "About data.overheid.nl", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "http://data.overheid.nl/en", "snippet": "Welkom op het Nationale Dataportaal van de Nederlandse overheid: data.overheid.nl. Op dit portaal wordt Nederlandse overheidsdata beschreven, dit kan zowel open als gesloten zijn.", "title": "Data register of the Dutch government | Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.digitaleoverheid.nl/nieuws/europese-data-act-van-toepassing-geworden/", "snippet": "De Data Act is samen met de Data Governance Act onderdeel van de Europese datastrategie. Het doel van de strategie: de EU wereldleider in datagedreven handelsactiviteiten maken en welvaart en welzijn binnen Europa vergroten. ... De Data Act zorgt ook voor een betere toegang tot hoogwaardige data. Het gaat daarbij om regels voor een ruimere beschikbaarheid van gegevens om innovatie, concurrentievermogen en de groei van de digitale economie van Europa te stimuleren. Daarnaast kunnen overheidsinstanties toegang krijgen tot data van derde partijen. Dit kan alleen bij een gerechtvaardigd doeleinde, zoals een noodsituatie.", "title": "Europese Data Act van toepassing geworden - Digitale Overheid", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://data.overheid.nl/en/impact-en", "snippet": "Impact is the effect that opening open data for reuse has to solve economic and social problems. Data.overheid.nl has several instruments to give insight in the impact of data: the applications that are developed using data; the high value datasets and statistics.", "title": "Impact of data | Data overheid", "provider": "diy"}]');
