INSERT OR IGNORE INTO phase2_researcher_runs (id,run_id,pair_run_id,question_id,country_code,retry_count,answer,answer_explanation,evidence_quote,source_url,retrieval_confidence,answer_confidence,search_queries_used,fetched_urls,domain_trust_score,language_route_used,notes,failure_mode,input_tokens,output_tokens,wall_clock_ms,estimated_cost_usd,condition_label,prompt_version_id,model_version,raw_response,created_at,search_provider_calls,experiment_id,search_snippets) VALUES (9191,'2206f8e0-e541-4243-8cd3-e3d74cb9edb3','fab2f1fb-c039-41d2-a841-6c643678740e','Q6','NL',2,'yes','The Netherlands aligns high-value datasets with harmonised INSPIRE themes and publishes them via APIs, interoperability measures beyond DCAT-AP tagging that support cross-country data exchange within the European Green Deal dataspace.','Samen met INSPIRE vormen de High Value Datasets (HVD) de basis voor de Europese Green Deal dataspace. Veel van de databronnen die in Nederland onder INSPIRE vallen, zijn ook opgenomen in de High Value Datasets (HVD) lijst. Wat verandert is dat deze databronnen nu dus ook via een API als open data beschikbaar komen.','https://www.geonovum.nl/nieuws/wat-betekent-de-uitvoeringsverordening-high-value-datasets-voor-dataproviders',0.85,0.62,'["Netherlands high-value datasets API standardisation EU interoperability framework", "hoogwaardige datasets Nederland Europese dataruimte semantische afstemming", "Geonovum Kadaster high-value datasets grensoverschrijdende uitwisseling INSPIRE"]','["https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s42979-024-02721-8", "https://wetransform.to/news-and-events/high-value-dataset-metadata/", "http://data.overheid.nl/en/community/maatschappij/high-value", "https://dataeuropa.gitlab.io/data-provider-manual/hvd/", "https://www.geonovum.nl/nieuws/wat-betekent-de-uitvoeringsverordening-high-value-datasets-voor-dataproviders", "https://docs.geostandaarden.nl/eu/handreiking-hvd/"]',0.3,'native',NULL,NULL,5720,974,15384,0.05295,'opus_o48',22,'claude-opus-4-8','The Netherlands is an EU member state, so `not_applicable` on country grounds doesn''t apply. The question asks about measures *besides* DCAT-AP tagging for cross-country interoperability.

