}','2026-07-12 18:30:28','[{"provider": "diy", "ms": 4464, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 15235, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 16604, "results": 0, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 10275, "results": 1, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 29722, "results": 3, "ok": true, "error": null}, {"provider": "diy", "ms": 26458, "results": 4, "ok": true, "error": null}]','exp36_model_opus','[{"url": "https://www.opengovpartnership.org/members/albania/commitments/AL0067/", "snippet": "According to the opinion poll \u2018Trust in government\u2019 of the citizens who have used the electronic services of e-Albania, 94.6% have found it functional and 80.1% find it easy to use. As a standard-compliant system based on international internet, the e-Albania portal is accessible from any device, including smartphones, televisions and digital kiosks in public places.", "title": "Provision of interactive electronic public services (AL0067)", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://akshi.gov.al/samiti-digjital-boteror-2025-repishti-me-e-albania-2-0-sherbime-me-te-avancuar-per-qytetaret-dhe-bizneset/", "snippet": "AKSHI, n\u00eb k\u00ebt\u00eb event, u p\u00ebrfaq\u00ebsua nga drejtuesja e platform\u00ebs e-Albania, Nevila Repishti, e cila evidentoi faktin se 95% e sh\u00ebrbimeve publike tani ofrohen ekskluzivisht online, s\u00eb bashku me risit\u00eb q\u00eb do t\u00eb sjell\u00eb e-Albania 2.0, nj\u00eb projekt i cili do t\u00eb realizohet n\u00eb bashk\u00ebpunim me Bank\u00ebn Bot\u00ebrore, p\u00ebr t\u00eb sjell\u00eb sh\u00ebrbime edhe m\u00eb t\u00eb avancuara p\u00ebr qytetar\u00ebt dhe bizneset. ... N\u00eb faz\u00ebn e par\u00eb, qytetar\u00ebt do t\u00eb mund t\u00eb p\u00ebrdorin aplikacionin p\u00ebr t\u00eb siguruar dokumente t\u00eb r\u00ebnd\u00ebsishme si karta e sh\u00ebndetit, certifikata personale, certifikata e lindjes, p\u00ebr t\u00eb vijuar m\u00eb von\u00eb edhe me 19 sh\u00ebrbime t\u00eb tjera elektronike. Gjithashtu, aplikacioni do t\u00eb mb\u00ebshtes\u00eb p\u00ebrdorimin e n\u00ebnshkrimit elektronik, duke ofruar mund\u00ebsin\u00eb e n\u00ebnshkrimit t\u00eb dokumenteve nga qytetar\u00ebt, administrata dhe bizneset.", "title": "https://akshi.gov.al/samiti-digjital-boteror-2025-...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://blogu.al/2025/11/sherbimet-e-reja-te-akshi-t-firme-elektronike-edhe-per-qytetaret/", "snippet": "Risi n\u00eb vendimin e qeveris\u00eb \u00ebsht\u00eb se u njihet e drejta edhe qytetar\u00ebve q\u00eb t\u00eb aplikojn\u00eb n\u00ebnshkrimin elektronik. Pra, tashm\u00eb nuk do jen\u00eb vet\u00ebm personat juridik, publik apo privat, por edhe individ\u00ebt t\u00eb cil\u00ebt mund t\u00eb p\u00ebrdorin k\u00ebt\u00eb sh\u00ebrbim. ... K\u00ebshtu, n\u00ebp\u00ebrmjet firm\u00ebs elektronike, qytetar\u00ebt mund t\u00eb n\u00ebnshkruajn\u00eb akte t\u00eb ndryshme dhe t\u00eb futen n\u00eb marr\u00ebdh\u00ebnie juridike pa qen\u00eb nevoja q\u00eb t\u00eb paraqiten personalisht duke shkurtuar k\u00ebshtu distancat fiizke e kohore q\u00eb nevojiteshin m\u00eb par\u00eb. ... VKM-ja rregullon llojet e sh\u00ebrbimeve elektronike dhe tarifat q\u00eb ofron AKSHI mbi n\u00ebnshkrimin elektronik, vul\u00ebn elektronike, certifikat\u00ebn elektronike p\u00ebr projektin e fiskalizimit, vul\u00ebn kohore si dhe transaksionin n\u00eb platform\u00ebn qeveritare t\u00eb nd\u00ebrveprimit (GG).", "title": "Sh\u00ebrbimet e reja t\u00eb AKSHI-t | Firm\u00eb elektronike edhe ... - Blogu", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://scantv.al/nga-e-hena-rikthehen-aplikimet-elektronike-per-lejet-e-ndertimit-akshi-ben-bilancin-nga-1225-sherbime-1214-jane-rikthyer", "snippet": "Aktualisht, sipas AKSHI-t, 1 mij\u00eb e 214 sh\u00ebrbime nga 1 mij\u00eb e 225 t\u00eb tilla mund t\u00eb p\u00ebrdoren nga qytetar\u00ebt dhe bizneset si m\u00eb par\u00eb. ... Duke nisur nga e h\u00ebna e ardhshme do t\u00eb mund t\u00eb aplikohet elektronikisht p\u00ebr lejet e nd\u00ebrtimit, duke rikthyer n\u00eb k\u00ebt\u00eb m\u00ebnyr\u00eb nj\u00eb nga sh\u00ebrbimet m\u00eb t\u00eb r\u00ebnd\u00ebsishme t\u00eb portalit qeveritar e-Albania. Kjo u b\u00eb e ditur nga Agjencia Komb\u00ebtare e Shoq\u00ebris\u00eb s\u00eb Informacionit, sipas s\u00eb cil\u00ebs, poothuajse t\u00eb gjitha sh\u00ebrbimet elektronike jan\u00eb normalisht t\u00eb aksesueshme. ... N\u00eb njoftimin p\u00ebr mediat, AKSHi deklaron se jan\u00eb n\u00eb funksion sh\u00ebrbimet p\u00ebr pasaportat, ndihm\u00ebn ekonomike, strehimin social dhe v\u00ebrtetimet e diplomave.", "title": "Nga e h\u00ebna, rikthehen aplikimet elektronike p\u00ebr lejet e ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.worldbank.org/en/region/eca/brief/digital-transformation-and-public-sector-reform-western-balkans-progress-toward-eu-accession-and-economic-growth", "snippet": "The World Bank and its partners are helping the Western Balkans accelerate reforms through programs such as Albania\u2019s GovTech initiative. Serbia is also working to strengthen public financial management for the green transition. A new regional program, supported by Austria through the Governance & Institutions Umbrella Program, will speed up digital government and public sector innovation, scale successful approaches across borders, and back key reforms for EU accession, deepening ongoing work i", "title": "Digital Transformation and Public Sector Reform: Western Balkans ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.worldbank.org/en/results/2025/07/03/transforming-institutions-for-inclusive-services-and-human-development-in-albania", "snippet": "The quality of digitally enabled services has improved, accompanied by increased service usage. Notably, service applications completed through the e-Albania portal and mobile application rose by 40 percent. The launch of the redesigned e-Albania 2.0 aimed to enhance accessibility, including for persons with disabilities, while newly adopted digital service standards have been rolled out to further strengthen service quality.", "title": "Transforming institutions for inclusive services and human ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2025/03/10/world-bank-approves-additional-support-to-advance-albania-s-public-service-transformation", "snippet": "The additional support builds on the progress of the Improving Equitable Access to High Standard Public Services through GovTech Program ($65 million), which aims to enhance the accessibility and quality of key public services. The project is currently supporting several activities, including the re-design and upgrading of the E-Albania platform -- a digital platform offering services to citizens and businesses, the establishment of Youth Innovation Centers to teach digital skills to youth, and  ... WASHINGTON, DC, March 10, 2025 \u2013The World Bank Group\u2019s Board of Executive Directors has approved an additional financing of $80 million to support Albania\u2019s ambitious public sector modernization and digital transformation agenda, further strengthening public sector modernization and improving access to essential services for citizens, particularly vulnerable groups. ... \u201cOur new support is expected to make a real difference in the lives of citizens. We project at least a 25% increase in the processing of online applications for public services, leading to improved access to services, including for vulnerable groups such as people with disabilities,\u201d said Simon Carl O\u2019Meally, Project Team Leader.", "title": "World Bank Approves Additional Support to Advance Albania''s ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.opengovpartnership.org/members/albania/commitments/al0062/", "snippet": "This commitment is tied to Albania\u2019s Digital Agenda 2015\u20132020 [13] and aims to further develop e-services for citizens and businesses in Albania. Currently, 591 out of 1,600 total government services are available electronically on the e-Albania portal. ... The e-Albania government portal, through various projects, has significantly\nincreased the number of electronic services, with a total of 1363 services\nout of which 590 electronic services. The e-Albania portal has been\ncreated on the principle of the Open Government Partnership and is\norientated towards the service to the citizens.", "title": "e-Government (AL0062) | Commitment from Albania", "provider": "diy"}]');
