eir datasets and upkeep is not consistent. In Albania, most of the provided data sets are from 2019, with a few exceptions. The latest updates from these institutions are made by the Ministry of Health and Social Protection, National Agency of ICT, AKSHI, and the Ministry of Finance and Economy (in 2024).", "title": "Data-Driven Governance: Strategies for Open Data in the ...", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://ndiqparate.al/?page_id=10789&lang=en", "snippet": "The information provided by AIS through its two portals, Spending Data Albania and Open Data Albania, contains all details about every payment, and treasury transaction carried out by the 1600 budgetary institutions in the country starting from January 2012. ... Treasury Transaction is a service provided by AIS for ensuring information, transparency, and civic monitoring and accountability. Such service enables taxpayers to learn how their tax money is spent by their government and public institutions.", "title": "Open Data Albania", "provider": "diy"}]');
