n that reuses terms from one or more base standards, adding more specificity by identifying mandatory, recommended and optional elements to be used for a particular application, as well as recommendations for controlled vocabularies to be used.", "title": "DCAT-AP 3.0", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/dcat-application-profile-data-portals-europe_en", "snippet": "- The Italian Digital Agency (AGID) with DCAT-AP_IT", "title": "DCAT Application Profile for data portals in Europe | ISA\u00b2", "provider": "diy"}, {"url": "https://www.agid.gov.it/en/news/agid-welcomes-european-data-community-20-countries-gather-rome-european-data-portal-workshop", "snippet": "The diverse European delegations exchanged practical methodologies and technical alignment challenges, specifically focusing on the GeoDCAT-AP specification and INSPIRE compliance standards, which are vital to achieving seamless interoperability across national data catalogs. ... The two-day event saw the active participation of institutional representatives from about twenty European countries, coming together to align on shared open data strategies and to strengthen transnational cooperation on public information assets.", "title": "20 Countries Gather in Rome for the European Data Portal Workshop", "provider": "diy"}]');
