The Researcher''s answer rests on the presence of open data initiatives, but the question asks whether open data is *having an impact* on transparency and accountability. The independent searches reveal substantial counter-evidence: systematic denial of FOI requests by public bodies, 750+ unanswered parliamentary questions, and OGP civil society assessments noting minimal dialogue and limited plan completion. These are documented failures in actual transparency and accountability outcomes, not mere infrastructure gaps. The Researcher should search for specific reuse cases and measurable outcomes to support the affirmative claim.','2026-07-12 13:13:19','exp32_model_haiku');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO phase2_verifier_runs (id,run_id,pair_run_id,question_id,country_code,retry_count,strategy_label,researcher_run_id,verdict,verifier_answer,verifier_confidence,substring_check_result,substring_check_notes,independent_search_queries,independent_evidence,rejection_reason,counter_evidence_quote,counter_source_url,suggested_search_query,failure_mode,input_tokens,output_tokens,wall_clock_ms,estimated_cost_usd,condition_label,prompt_version_id,model_version,raw_response,created_at,experiment_id) VALUES (5022,'d33b591d-8bc1-41bb-b348-3970d734682e','cb4719f0-889e-4d9c-9638-5d85194f34af','I22','MT',1,'verifier-disprove',8342,'pass','no',0.85,'pass','matched against snippet 0 the Researcher read (1 fragment(s))','["Malta open data environmental impact quantified results", "Malta climate change open data reuse assessment study", "Impatt tal-open data fuq l-ambjent Malta"]','["DOMINICAN REPUBLIC Carbon Footprint Calculator for Public Procurement: Committed to creating a Carbon Footprint Calculator to quantify the environmental impact of public procurement projects, which will be available to the public and will play a role in future contracting decisions in the medium ter", "Today, the EIB released its seventh annual Climate Survey, which presents the views of over 24 000 respondents from across the European Union and the United States on the topic of climate change. In Malta, 500 people took part in the survey, which was conducted in August 2024.", "Is-sa\u0127\u0127a tal-pjanti g\u0127andha rwol kru\u010bjali biex i\u017c\u017comm ambjent bilan\u010bjat u sostenibbli. Meta l-pjanti jkunu f''sa\u0127\u0127ithom, huma jipprovdu benefi\u010b\u010bji numeru\u017ci. Dawn jinkludu arja aktar nadifa, kwalit\u00e0 tal-ilma mtejba, u abitats g\u0127al fawna selva\u0121\u0121a."]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5996,587,9696,0.008931,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
