ataset implementing regulation (HVD IR). The document is called the \"usage guidelines of DCAT-AP for High-Value Datasets\", in short DCAT-AP HVD. It means that thes", "Which metadata standard is supported by your portal? | E.g. DCAT-AP, CKAN JSON, or INSPIRE", "Enhancing data quality, accessibility, and reusability across government. ... Quality Assurance: Monitoring data quality, ensuring datasets are up-to-date, correctly stored, and meet required standards.", "Metadata policies define how metadata is created and governed per data quality and compliance standards. These policies provide clear guidelines for structuring metadata across all data assets. As a result, they improve metadata quality and reliability by strictly ensuring it complies with regulator", "The following metadata is required for NSIPs and the ERPD according to Articles 5-8 of the Data Governance Act: title, description, publisher, conditions for re-use / access procedure, format, and size. To enable a comprehensive harvesting of required metadata, equivalent metadata is mandatory for E"]','The evidence quote is generic and does not establish that Malta has *set* specific metadata quality standards that data providers must abide by. The phrase ''meet required standards'' is vague and does not confirm the existence of enforceable standards (e.g., mandatory DCAT-AP properties, licence requirements, or minimum metadata fields). The Researcher''s independent searches returned only generic DCAT-AP information and best-practice guides, with no Malta-specific metadata mandate or standard. The DGU quote describes quality assurance as a goal, not proof of implemented standards.','Quality Assurance: Monitoring data quality, ensuring datasets are up-to-date, correctly stored, and meet required standards.','https://opm.gov.mt/en/public-bodies/data-governance-unit-dgu/','Malta open data portal metadata requirements mandatory DCAT-AP properties licence fields',NULL,6124,853,11075,0.010388999999999999,'haiku_h