y Open State Foundation and Weyeser shows that the Dutch government portal, data.overheid.nl, refers to 5,714 datasets containing 8,159 files, however, only 3.3% give a valid response when accessed. The bulk of public sector information on the government portal refers to links of the natio", "It is possible that a data set on data.overheid.nl is displayed as ''closed''. This means that the dataset is not or will not be openly available. If a data set is shown as ''closed'', it must be indicated why the dataset is not available and will not be available."]','The evidence does not demonstrate that data.overheid.nl itself offers a native preview function for geospatial data. The cited example links to an external ArcGIS viewer hosted by a province (South-Holland), not a built-in portal feature. The independent search results show that geospatial data on data.overheid.nl typically requires external tools (ArcGis, QGis) or separate services (PDOK) to preview, and that many datasets have broken or unavailable links. No evidence establishes that the national portal (data.overheid.nl) has integrated geospatial preview functionality.','WMS is used in many GEO datasets. Querying a web service format can cause problems in the web browser. A help tool such as ArcGis or QGis is therefore advisable when opening the data.','https://data.overheid.nl/dataset/54778-metrex-borders-eu-2024','data.overheid.nl native geospatial preview map viewer built-in feature',NULL,6058,998,11933,0.011047999999999999,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
