dt meegenomen in bijvoorbeeld beleidsvorming voor landbouw en ruimtelijke inrichting, krijgt ", "De biodiversiteitsvoetafdruk van Nederlandse consumptie is tussen 2010 en 2021 afgenomen met 20 procent. De biodiversiteitsvoetafdruk van Nederlandse productie lag in 2021 ongeveer 6 procent lager dan in 2010. De biodiversiteitsvoetafdrukken geven aan hoeveel biodiversiteitsverlies er mondiaal optre"]','The evidence quote describes what the Environmental Data Compendium is (a comprehensive overview platform), but does not establish that open data is actually having a demonstrated impact on biodiversity protection or environmental quality outcomes. The Researcher conflates the existence of a data platform with proven impact. The question specifically asks whether open data is ''having an impact'' on biodiversity protection—a causal claim requiring evidence of outcomes, not merely evidence of data availability. Additionally, the Researcher acknowledges that no discrete reuse case with URLs was found, yet the explanation section explicitly requires (1) a URL to a reuse case, (2) a URL to the dataset, and (3) a description with impact evidence. These required elements are absent.','The Researcher notes acknowledge: ''the search results do not provide a single discrete reuse case with URLs as requested in the explanation section.'' This is a material gap for a question explicitly requiring reuse case documentation and impact demonstration.','https://www.cbs.nl/en-gb/society/nature-and-environment/environmental-data-compendium','Netherlands open data reuse case biodiversity conservation measurable impact example',NULL,6225,1037,12892,0.01141,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
