    "Gegevens, Informatie en Kennis | Biodiversiteit.NL — NLBIF ''Netherlands Biodiversity Information Facility'', het Nederlandse kennisknooppunt van GBIF (''Global Biodiversity Information Facility'') t.b.v. het open en vrij toegankelijk maken van mondiale bio"
  ],
  "rejection_reason": "The evidence quote describes what the Environmental Data Compendium is (a comprehensive overview platform), but does not establish that open data is actually having a demonstrated impact on biodiversity protection or environmental quality outcomes. The Researcher conflates the existence of a data platform with proven impact. The question specifically asks whether open data is ''having an impact'' on biodiversity protection—a causal claim requiring evidence of outcomes, not merely evidence of data availability. Additionally, the Researcher acknowledges that no discrete reuse case with URLs was found, yet the explanation section explicitly requires (1) a URL to a reuse case, (2) a URL to the dataset, and (3) a description with impact evidence. These required elements are absent.",
  "counter_evidence_quote": "The Researcher notes acknowledge: ''the search results do not provide a single discrete reuse case with URLs as requested in the explanation section.'' This is a material gap for a question explicitly requiring reuse case documentation and impact demonstration.",
