sed and is made available in a machine-readable format. Statistics Netherlands provides three different types of open data. The OData interfaces (APIs) of Statistics Netherlands enable users to use data in automated processes.", "Welkom op het Nationale Dataportaal van de Nederlandse overheid: data.overheid.nl. Op dit portaal wordt Nederlandse overheidsdata beschreven, dit kan zowel open als gesloten zijn.", "Open Data Nederland\nDescription\nA community hub for Open Data in the Netherlands.", "Inmiddels zijn meer dan 12.000 datasets te vinden op de data.overheid.nl."]','The Researcher''s claim answers a narrower question than what was asked. The evidence shows that the portal displays datasets marked as ''closed'' and indicates reasons why they cannot be made available. However, the question asks specifically whether users can ''see what data exists but cannot be made available as open data'' — i.e., whether the portal provides visibility into data that exists within government but is restricted. The evidence conflates two separate concepts: (1) descriptions of closed datasets (which may be metadata about the restrictions themselves), and (2) actual inventory of existing-but-restricted data. The independent search snippets confirm the portal shows ''closed'' datasets with reasoning, but do not confirm that users can browse a comprehensive inventory of government-held data that exists but is unavailable. The distinction matters: showing why specific disclosed datasets are closed is different from showing users what undisclosed datasets exist but cannot be released.','It is possible that a data set on data.overheid.nl is displayed as ''closed''. This means that the dataset is not or will not be openly available.','https://data.overheid.nl/en/ondersteuning/zoeken-data','data.overheid.nl inventory restricted datasets exist but unavailable Dutch government',NULL,6148,622,8347,0.009257999999999999,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
