ditional mandatory and optional metadata elements in addition to existing, required DCAT-AP metadata elements.", "To access the published company data, the STIRData platform, as well as any other application searching for the data, only needs to know the URLs of their respective SPARQL endpoints. These can be found in a data catalogue listing the STIRData compliant datasets, e.g., in the Official Portal for Eur", "Harmonising the implementation of the re-use conditions of high-value datasets entails the technical specification for making the datasets available in a machine-readable format and via application programming interfaces (APIs). Making high-value datasets available under optimal conditions strengthe", "Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/138 aims to maximize the availability and usability of public data to achieve economic, social and environmental benefits, increase administrative efficiency and improve the transparency and accountability of public bodies. The aim is to establish harmonized standar", "Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/138 has started applying. This implementing regulation establishes a list of High-Value datasets in the context of the EU Open Data Directive that called for priority release of particularly valuable data assets. High-Value datasets are defined as data wh", "The absence of a Member State HVD contact or national coordination has a substantial impact on the correct application of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/138 on HVDs (HVD IR) in the Member State."]','The evidence quote is a generic principle about standards adoption and does not specifically confirm implementation of measures beyond DCAT-AP for high-value dataset interoperability. The Researcher cites ''snippet 2'' and ''snippet 4'' as supporting implementation of multiple content standards and a Data bij de Bron program, but these snippets were not provided in the independent search results, making verification impossible. The question specifically asks about measures beyond DCAT-AP to ensure high-value datasets (EU 2023/138) are interoperable with datasets of other countries; the quoted evidence does not demonstrate this.','Conformance with the DCAT-AP HVD profile requires compliance with DCAT-AP as a prerequisite. The HVD profile defines additional mandatory and optional metadata elements in addition to existing requirements.','https://data.europa.eu/api/hub/store/dataset/dcat-ap-high-value-datasets/5bfcd87c-ae10-4a51-8e55-6b32e19f6e1e','Netherlands Data bij de Bron program interoperability standards high-value datasets implementation',NULL,6226,946,10856,0.010955999999999999,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
