ebrdorimin e informacionit t\u00eb sektorit publik\", \u00ebsht\u00eb nj\u00eb akt ligjor i r\u00ebnd\u00ebsish\u00ebm n\u00eb Republik\u00ebn e Shqip\u00ebris\u00eb, i cili synon t\u00eb promovoj\u00eb transparenc\u00ebn, llogaridh\u00ebnien dhe inovacionin p\u00ebrmes aksesit t\u00eb lir\u00eb n\u00eb t\u00eb dh\u00ebnat publike. Ky ligj p\u00ebrcakton kuadr"]','The Researcher answered ''no'' based on absence of evidence in the OECD source, but the independent search results provide direct counter-evidence. Snippet [1] references a questionnaire-based data collection process by idp.al (a credible Albanian institution) addressing 312 public institutions with a 77% response rate—this is a concrete monitoring mechanism. Snippet [2] indicates the Albanian Data Protection Commissioner''s office has published an implementation report on Law 33/2022 (open data law), which constitutes a formal monitoring process. These sources demonstrate that Albania does have processes in place to monitor open data reuse.','According to data collected through a questionnaire addressed to 312 institutions, with a response rate of about 77%, an increasing commitment of public bodies towards transparency and data publication','https://idp.al/','Albania idp.al open data monitoring report 2023 2024',NULL,6074,717,8464,0.009659000000000001,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
