 of the re-use conditions of high-value datasets entails the technical specification for making the datasets available in a machine-readable format and via application programming interfaces (APIs). Making high-value datasets available under optimal conditions strengthe", "Sinds 9 juni 2024 zijn de nieuwe EU-regels van kracht om meer openbare datasets beschikbaar te stellen voor hergebruik. Deze zogenaamde ''hoogwaardige datasets'' in de zin van Uitvoeringsverordening 2023/138 bevatten informatie over zes thematische gebieden die zijn vastgelegd in de richtlijn Open Dat"]','The Researcher''s answer of ''inconclusive'' cannot be accepted because the question requires a definitive yes/no answer about implementation of measures beyond DCAT-AP. While the Researcher correctly identified that the cited Dutch legislation snippet does not directly answer the specific question, they should have conducted more targeted verification of Netherlands-specific implementation measures (such as consulting Dutch government open data policy documents, the official Dutch DCAT-AP implementation guidance, or national data strategies) before defaulting to ''inconclusive''. The independent search results confirm that EU 2023/138 requires harmonized technical specifications, but do not reveal Netherlands-specific supplementary measures beyond DCAT-AP. A committed yes/no answer requires affirmative evidence of additional measures, not absence of evidence.','Harmonising the implementation of the re-use conditions of high-value datasets entails the technical specification for making the datasets available in a machine-readable format and via application protocols','https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/138/oj','Netherlands DCAT-AP implementation high-value datasets 2024 national guidelines additional measures',NULL,6147,660,7761,0.009447,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
