ata by Competent Authorities (\"Guidance\"), marking an important step toward operationalising Law No. 124/2024, Albania''s GDPR-aligned data protection law. This guidance introduces esse"]','The Researcher''s answer of ''inconclusive'' is justified, but the evidence provided does not actually support a confident ''inconclusive'' verdict for this specific question. The OGP commitment describes future plans (''will make available'', ''develop strategies'') rather than concrete actions already taken. The independent searches reveal no evidence of implemented support mechanisms, only planned commitments and unrelated technical assistance programs. The question asks whether concrete actions were taken; the evidence only shows that actions were planned or committed to. This distinction is material to the answer.','This commitment will make available new data from additional public institutions, as well as develop strategies to improve citizens understanding of the use and application of the Open Data Portal — this describes a future commitment, not concrete actions already taken.','https://www.opengovpartnership.org/members/albania/commitments/AL0079/','Albania open data portal technical support implementation 2023 2024 2025 concrete actions',NULL,5939,691,9165,0.009394,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
