ks to the public domain by waiving all", "An open licence is one that places very few restrictions on what you can do with the content or data that is being licensed. According to the Open Definition, There are only two kinds of restrictions that an open licence can place: that you must give attribution to the source of the content or data ", "This page provides an overview of copyright rules of Albania relevant to uploading works into Wikimedia Commons. Note that any work originating in Albania must be in the public domain, or available under a free license, in both Albania and the United States before it can be uploaded to Wikimedia Com"]','The Researcher cites a LinkedIn post as the primary source for an official Albanian government guideline (Joint Guideline No. 2, Feb 2025). While the substring check passes, the LinkedIn post is not an authoritative source for verifying official government open data policy. The actual text of the Joint Guideline itself was not retrieved or quoted. The independent search queries returned no corroborating results about this specific Albanian guideline, its content, or whether it specifically recommends CC0 and CC BY 4.0. The evidence does not directly confirm the specific question about CC licences being recommended.','No independent search results confirmed the existence or content of the February 2025 Albanian Joint Guideline referenced in the LinkedIn post.',NULL,'site:gov.al OR site:drejtaperfituesit.al ''Udhëzimi i Përbashkët'' 2025 licencë të dhënat e hapura',NULL,6239,717,9750,0.009824,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
