ion that provides the complete legal foundation. ..", "The OPEN Government Data Act (Title II of the Foundations for Evidence-Based Policymaking Act of 2018, P.L. 115-435) requires agencies to make their data publicly available in open, machine-readable formats and to apply open licenses so that if data are made public there are no restrictions on copyi"]','The Researcher''s evidence quote does not appear verbatim in any of the retrieved snippets. The claim of ''inconclusive'' is supported by the low retrieval and answer confidence scores, but the methodology is flawed: the Researcher provided a paraphrased summary rather than a direct citation from an authoritative source. Snippet [8] from the Albanian Open Data Portal mentions global norms for publishing open data but does not provide specific details about CC licensing recommendations. The Researcher did not successfully locate Albania''s actual open data guidelines or licensing policy.','Ensuring that the data on the Open Data Portal meets the globally agreed norms for publishing open data, as follows: 1. open by default 2. timely and comprehensive 3. accessible and usable 4. comparab','https://opendata.gov.al/','site:opendata.gov.al license OR licensa OR Creative Commons policy guidelines',NULL,6290,652,9951,0.00955,'haiku_h45',23,'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001','```json
