INSERT OR IGNORE INTO phase2_verifier_runs (id,run_id,pair_run_id,question_id,country_code,retry_count,strategy_label,researcher_run_id,verdict,verifier_answer,verifier_confidence,substring_check_result,substring_check_notes,independent_search_queries,independent_evidence,rejection_reason,counter_evidence_quote,counter_source_url,suggested_search_query,failure_mode,input_tokens,output_tokens,wall_clock_ms,estimated_cost_usd,condition_label,prompt_version_id,model_version,raw_response,created_at,experiment_id) VALUES (5295,'2206f8e0-e541-4243-8cd3-e3d74cb9edb3','7252fad3-b480-40a6-ae2b-a53e5ac5e850','P13','MT',0,'verifier-disprove',8959,'pass','yes',0.78,'pass','matched against snippet 0 the Researcher read (1 fragment(s))','["Malta open data governance struttura ta'' tmexxija nieqsa", "Malta open data portal stakeholder participation missing", "Malta data governance council abolished discontinued"]','["The Data Governance Unit (DGU) operates within the Office of the Prime Minister and is led by the Chief Data Officer (CDO). It was established to strengthen the strategic management, interoperability, and quality of data across the Public Administration. The DGU serves as the central authority for d", "During implementation, the MoJ reconvened the MSF only once in February 2024, did not update the OGP webpage, and declined civil society requests for meetings.[8] These shortcomings led to the withdrawal of civil society stakeholders from the process, including the Daphne Caruana Galizia Foundation,"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,3938,833,12857,0.040515,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','Let me evaluate this claim.

**Substring check:** PASS — verbatim found.

**Source authority:** opm.gov.mt (Office of the Prime Minister, Malta) is authoritative and not forbidden.

**Evidence fit:** The quote describes the Data Governance Council including "representatives from key entities having a stake in Data Governance throughout Public Administration." This confirms a governance structure. However, the question asks specifically about inclusion of "various open data stakeholders" — the quote refers to entities within Public Administration, i.e., internal government bodies, not necessarily broader open-data stakeholders (civil society, private sector, academia). Still, a governance structure enabling participation of stakeholders is described.

**Counter-evidence:** Snippet [2] mentions OGP shortcomings — MSF reconvened only once, declined civil society meetings. This concerns the Open Government Partnership multi-stakeholder forum, not the DGU/Data Governance Council. It doesn''t directly contradict the existence of the Data Governance Council structure. It''s a different body.

The claim answers "yes" — a governance structure enabling stakeholder participation exists. The cited source supports the existence of the Data Governance Council with stakeholder representatives. This satisfies the criterion.

