.", "Similarly to the Indian case, i.e., with the focus on local governments and their data opening, in 2016, data.overheid.nl (the Netherlands), a Municipal High-Value List has been compiled by the national government in collaboration with municipalities, the Digital Urban Agenda, and VNG/KING, intended", "The tables which can be viewed and downloaded in StatLine are also available as open data. The collection of datasets can be searched in the StatLine data portal. All datasets from StatLine are also part of the open data collection of the Dutch government, called data.overheid.nl (Dutch)."]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4528,653,10628,0.038965,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','All four checks pass. Substring verified verbatim, source is the official Dutch government portal support page (authoritative, non-forbidden), the quote directly answers the question (only government organisations approved as data owner), and independent snippets corroborate ([3] "Overheidsorganisaties publiceren hier", [4] "Overheidsorganisaties kunnen datasets aanmelden").

