ndom het beschikbaar stellen van open data in de geo-sector is af te lezen aan het aantal datasets dat sinds 2008 in het nationaal georegister (NGR) is gepubliceerd. Hoewel dat strikt genomen geen open data register is, wordt daar in de praktijk weinig gesloten data gepubliceerd. .", "Een groot aantal datasets op het open dataportaal van de Nederlandse overheid verwijst naar gebroken links. Onderzoek van Open State toont aan dat links die verwijzen naar het Nationaal Georegister niet goed functioneren. ... Op het open dataportaal van de Nederlandse overheid staat vermeldt dat het", "The online portal https://data.overheid.nl serves as the central access point for all government data. ... By introducing and using data.overheid.nl as the open government data portal, the quality of open data, in terms of meeting the same standards and opening data in the same manner, has improved,", "Data.overheid.nl assists government organisations in opening all available data. We also support data re-users in finding specific open data sets. Data that is not (yet) available as open data can be made available through a data request. ... Data.overheid.nl is a register and offers help with openi", "It is possible that a data set on data.overheid.nl is displayed as ''closed''. This means that the dataset is not or will not be openly available. If a data set is shown as ''closed'', it must be indicated why the dataset is not available and will not be available.", "Closed data sets\nSome data sets on data.overheid.nl are ''closed''. This means that the data set is not or will not be available for public reuse. If a data set is ''closed'', it must also be clear why a data set is not available or will not become available. Read more here."]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4695,663,13553,0.04005,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','All four checks pass. Substring verified. Source is authoritative (data.overheid.nl is the national portal itself — not a forbidden ODMI source). Evidence directly answers 