INSERT OR IGNORE INTO phase2_verifier_runs (id,run_id,pair_run_id,question_id,country_code,retry_count,strategy_label,researcher_run_id,verdict,verifier_answer,verifier_confidence,substring_check_result,substring_check_notes,independent_search_queries,independent_evidence,rejection_reason,counter_evidence_quote,counter_source_url,suggested_search_query,failure_mode,input_tokens,output_tokens,wall_clock_ms,estimated_cost_usd,condition_label,prompt_version_id,model_version,raw_response,created_at,experiment_id) VALUES (5406,'2206f8e0-e541-4243-8cd3-e3d74cb9edb3','fab2f1fb-c039-41d2-a841-6c643678740e','Q6','NL',3,'verifier-disprove',9201,'pass','inconclusive',0.7,'pass','matched against snippet 0 the Researcher read (1 fragment(s))','["Nederland high-value datasets interoperabiliteit grensoverschrijdend maatregelen", "Netherlands high-value datasets cross-border interoperability implementation", "hoogwaardige datasets 2023/138 Nederland interoperabiliteit metadata standaarden"]','["High value datasets are datasets that hold significant value for society. These are made available with priority by government organisations and are also published on data.overheid.nl. A distinction is made between two types of high value datasets:\nHoogwaardige dataset | EU: datasets that belong to ", "Further to the Open Data Directive that set the legal framework for open data, based on the key principles of transparency and fair competition, the Commission adopted in 2023 Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/138 laying down a list of concrete high-value datasets (HVDs) and the arrangements for the", "The Netherlands is not starting from zero. Far from it. Over the past years, Dutch healthcare has made meaningful progress in data exchange. Medication records, GP referrals, and acute care transfers are all examples of areas where interoperability is already improving in practice. ... That aligns w", "The FDS is not a centralized system. Instead, it connects data providers and users through a shared set of agreements, standards and governance functions. Its core principles \u2014 such as data sovereignty, minimal data exchange, and federation \u2014 align closely with European ambitions for interoperable, ", "Harmonising the implementation of the re-use conditions of high-value datasets entails the technical specification for making the datasets available in a machine-readable format and via application programming interfaces (APIs). Making high-value datasets available under optimal conditions strengthe", "Sinds 9 juni 2024 zijn de nieuwe EU-regels van kracht om meer openbare datasets beschikbaar te stellen voor hergebruik. Deze zogenaamde ''hoogwaardige datasets'' in de zin van Uitvoeringsverordening 2023/138 bevatten informatie over zes thematische gebieden die zijn vastgelegd in de richtlijn Open Dat", "Er zijn verschillende standaarden voor verschillende typen metadata en verschillende domeinen. Voor beschrijvende metadata zijn er bijvoorbeeld de standaarden MODS en Dublin Core. Voor preserveringsmetadata bestaan bijvoorbeeld PREMIS en MIX. ... Als een organisatie verzuimt om geldende metadatastan"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4607,796,15198,0.042935,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','The Researcher answered "inconclusive" with low answer confidence. The evidence quote is generic and does not address additional interoperability measures for high-value datasets. The independent snippets also don''t confirm a specific "yes" or "no" answer about additional measures beyond DCAT-AP tagging.

The evidence is genuinely insufficient to confirm yes or no. The Researcher''s inconclusive verdict is well-grounded and defensible. The cited source passes substring check and is authoritative (government portal), but simply doesn''t answer the specific question — which is exactly why inconclusive is appropriate.

