r supplied no definitional text (e.g. the relevant definitions article of the law), and the Researcher''s own notes concede no verbatim definition was quoted.','no verbatim definition text of ''reuse'' itself is quoted in the snippets','https://idp.al/2026/04/21/te-dhenat-e-hapura-dhe-riperdorimi-i-informacionit-publik-ne-shqiperi-progres-i-dukshem-por-sfida-perpara/','ligji 33/2022 Shqipëri neni përkufizime ''ripërdorim'' informacioni sektorit publik',NULL,4076,1031,16912,0.046155,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','The Researcher''s evidence confirms a law titled about open data and reuse exists, but the question asks specifically whether a *definition of open data reuse* exists. The cited quote is just the law''s title — it does not contain a definition of "reuse." The Researcher''s own notes admit no verbatim definition text is quoted.

However, the independent snippets [2] and [3] confirm the law 33/2022 explicitly governs "ripërdorimin e informacionit të sektorit publik" (reuse of public sector information), and such transposition laws (based on EU Directive 2019/1024) contain a definition of "reuse." The law''s existence and scope strongly imply a legal definition exists.

The evidence gap: the Researcher cited only the title, not the definitional article. But the answer "yes" is well-supported by the fact that a dedicated transposition law exists that by design contains a reuse definition.

