gov.al/) currently provides open data from several sectors \u2013 for example: health, treasury, customs, education, business etc. This commitment will improve scale up the volume and quality of open data available on the Government\u2019s open data portal. ... Bas"]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,4125,641,11659,0.03665,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','The Researcher''s evidence quote is about the general Digital Agenda strategy and doesn''t address metadata currency. However, snippet [2] from an Albania Open Data Policy explicitly states data assets "shall be periodically updated (semi-annually or at least annually)" — this is counter-evidence suggesting a pre-defined approach may exist. But this concerns data updates, not specifically metadata currency, and I lack the full authoritative source confirming a metadata-specific update process.

