ve n\u00eb privilegje.\n- Primare\nT\u00eb dh\u00ebnat mblidhen n\u00eb burim, me nivelin m\u00eb t\u00eb lart\u00eb t\u00eb mundsh\u00ebm t\u00eb granularitetit, jo n\u00eb fo", "Gjat\u00eb dit\u00ebs s\u00eb par\u00eb, kushtuar rip\u00ebrdorimit t\u00eb informacionit t\u00eb sektorit publik, p\u00ebrfaq\u00ebsueset e Zyr\u00ebs s\u00eb Komisionerit zhvilluan prezantimin e par\u00eb t\u00eb seminarit, duke paraqitur kuadrin ligjor shqiptar p\u00ebr t\u00eb dh\u00ebnat e hapura dhe rip\u00ebrdorimin e informacionit publik, si dhe masat e nd\u00ebrmarra p\u00ebr ngritje"]','The cited evidence quote concerns dataset publication under OGP Commitment 6 and does not mention any deployment-quality assessment model (5-Star or FAIR), so it does not answer the question about whether Albania uses such a model. The evidence fails the evidence-fit test; independent snippets [1] and [2] hint that a 5-Star/FAIR model may in fact be applied to Western Balkans portals including Albania, meaning the cited quote is both irrelevant and potentially points to a different answer.','Application to the Western Balkans National Open Data Portals — | Star rate | Description of stars (metrics) |','https://www.opengovpartnership.org/documents/albania-action-plan-review-2023-2025/','Albania national open data portal 5-star rating FAIR assessment AKSHI official',NULL,4285,1235,22337,0.0523,'opus_o48',23,'claude-opus-4-8','Looking at the evidence, I need to verify whether Albania uses a model like 5-Star or FAIR to assess deployment quality.

The Researcher''s quote about "Commitment 6 continues the publication of datasets" says nothing about a quality-assessment model. It''s about dataset publication, not deployment-quality assessment. The evidence does not fit the question at all.

The independent snippets are more revealing:
- [1] Shows a 5-Star rating applied to Western Balkans National Open Data Portals (which includes Albania)
- [2] References a WorldFAIR project involving Albania implementing FAIR principles
- [3] Albania''s OGP open-data guide referencing open-data principles

These snippets suggest the 5-Star model may in fact be applied to Albania''s portal, which points toward "yes" rather than "inconclusive" — but the snippets are fragmentary and don''t clearly establish that Albania itself uses such a model to assess deployment quality (the [1] snippet describes an external application to Western Balkans portals, not necessarily an official national self-assessment).

The Researcher''s cited evidence does not support any answer to this question (evidence-fit failure). While I lean toward the answer being potentially "yes" given the independent snippets, none of the evidence — Researcher''s or mine — is decisive enough to confidently confirm an official national deployment-quality model. The Researcher''s evidence quote is simply irrelevant to the question.

Since the cited evidence doesn''t address the question at all, and no confident answer can be reached, I agree the answer is inconclusive but the verdict must fail on evidence fit.

